**Dr. Tomori** (Secondary). An AI pioneer, believed dead, who uploaded
his mind into the Malicron Corporation's network. Dr. Heiji Tomori, a
groundbreaking artificial-intelligence researcher, was recruited as
the lone man at the Malicron Corporation, where his work made the
company's long-held dream, Project MIHO, real. Soon afterward he was
killed in an accident -- or so everyone believes. Drawing on his
expertise with artificial brains, he had copied his entire mind into
Malicron's network. Unknown to anyone, he quietly steers the company's
work and searches the world's networks for any sign of his beloved
Miho. *Knowledge (AI) +5, Knowledge (Robotics) +4, Smart +4, Unique
Ability (Instant Computer Research) +3; Absent-Minded −1, Unique
Weakness (Can Only Travel in Cyberspace) −3, Unique Weakness (No
Physical Form) −3.* Litany of Scientific Fact (Affinity: Erudite;
Fatiguing): Roll 2, DX 1, End 0. Dr. Tomori's exhaustive knowledge can
be tiresome to the uninitiated. Defense 2. Health 20, Endurance 20.
TV 1.

